depgraph: share the _flatten_atoms() cache between backtracking attempts

Sub-series: L (flatten-atoms memo) - patch 1 of 1; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.
Ported to upstream 73646c35d: adapted: upstream's _flatten_atoms() has a keys parameter and the cache key (pkg, use, keys); the key is kept, only the dict moves to _frozen_config

The cache of _flatten_atoms() (use_reduce of a package's dependency
strings for a USE set) moves from the per-attempt state to _frozen_config,
so that backtracking attempts share it. The result is a pure function of
(pkg, use), since the metadata of a Package does not change. Exceptions
are not cached, as before.

This was one of the pieces of patch 0025 of the 25-patch ladder
(config-trims-and-leftovers), which is now patches 0022, 0025, 0026, 0027
and 0030. The pieces were not measured one by one in the ladder; together,
on top of patches 0001-0024: sum of six states 95.9 -> 90.5 s (-5.5 s,
-1.2 % of the stock sum 447.5). Alone on stock 3.0.83: see README
(sub-series L).

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
isolated from the full patch and measured on 2026-11-20..21; cut out of its
former patch on 2026-11-21 without changing a line of code. Not a
human-written change. Base: Portage 3.0.83. Test: `emerge -p -uND @world` on
six states of one system image, one resolve at a time; every run gave the
same merge list in the same order, the same number of backtracking attempts
and the same package count as unpatched 3.0.83.
---
--- a/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
+++ b/lib/_emerge/depgraph.py
@@ -437,1 +437,4 @@
-        self._highest_license_masked = {}
+        # (pkg, USE flags, dependency variables) -> frozenset of atoms, see
+        # depgraph._flatten_atoms.
+        self._flatten_atoms_cache = {}
+        self._highest_license_masked = {}
@@ -820,7 +823,6 @@
         self._ignored_deps = []
         self._highest_pkg_cache = {}
         self._highest_pkg_cache_cp_map = {}
-        self._flatten_atoms_cache = {}
         self._changed_deps_pkgs = {}
 
         # Binary packages that have been rejected because they
@@ -3531,10 +3533,17 @@
         @return: set of evaluated atoms
         """
 
+        # The result is use_reduce() of the package's dependency strings
+        # with the given USE, its IUSE and its EAPI: a pure function of
+        # (pkg, use, keys), since the metadata of a Package does not change
+        # (keys: upstream, after 3.0.83). So
+        # the cache is kept in _frozen_config, where all backtracking runs
+        # share it (they ask for the same packages again), instead of in
+        # _dynamic_config. Exceptions are not cached, as before.
         cache_key = (pkg, use, keys)
 
         try:
-            return self._dynamic_config._flatten_atoms_cache[cache_key]
+            return self._frozen_config._flatten_atoms_cache[cache_key]
         except KeyError:
             pass
 
@@ -3559,5 +3568,5 @@
         atoms = frozenset(atoms)
 
-        self._dynamic_config._flatten_atoms_cache[cache_key] = atoms
+        self._frozen_config._flatten_atoms_cache[cache_key] = atoms
         return atoms
 
